- Added Google conditional access device registration (Fleet Premium): company-owned iOS, iPadOS, and Android hosts sign in to Google through fleetdm.com, and Fleet stores the host's Google device users and marks them as managed with the customer's service account. Added the device status routes, the `POST /api/v1/fleet/google_conditional_access/register` route that fleetdm.com calls, and a cron that unmarks hosts deleted or unenrolled from Fleet, retries failed marks, and marks hosts registered with the Google bookmark flow.
- Changed `PUT /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/google_device_id` to require Google conditional access to be connected and a company-owned host, and to mark the device's users as managed in Google. `DELETE /api/v1/fleet/hosts/:id/google_device_id` now also unmarks them. A host's `google_device_id` is also set when its end user signs in to Google.
